Error: `notes` is a `Table<String, String>`, and only an `HttpClient` replies
   ╭─[ requirements/main.req.inset:3:9 ]
   │
 3 │     and notes["GET /x"] replies OK
   │         ──┬──  
   │           ╰──── not a client
   │ 
   │ Help: `replies` sets up how a fake `HttpClient` answers a call
───╯
Error: expected a call, such as `"GET /forecast/London"`
   ╭─[ requirements/main.req.inset:4:17 ]
   │
 4 │     and weather["FETCH forecast"] replies OK
   │                 ────────┬───────  
   │                         ╰───────── a call is its method and path, in one string
   │ 
   │ Help: write the method, `GET`, `POST`, `PUT` or `DELETE`, a space, and the path from the client's base address, starting with `/`
───╯
Error: unknown status `Fine`
   ╭─[ requirements/main.req.inset:5:35 ]
   │
 5 │     and weather["GET /y"] replies Fine
   │                                   ──┬─  
   │                                     ╰─── not an HTTP status
   │ 
   │ Help: write a status by its standard name, such as `OK`, `NotFound` or `Conflict`
───╯
Error: a reply's body is text, written as a string
   ╭─[ requirements/main.req.inset:6:43 ]
   │
 6 │     and weather["GET /z"] replies OK with 3
   │                                           ┬  
   │                                           ╰── expected a string
───╯
Error: `replies` follows `given`
    ╭─[ requirements/main.req.inset:35:9 ]
    │
 35 │     and weather["GET /health"] replies OK
    │         ────────────────┬────────────────  
    │                         ╰────────────────── this sets up how a call is answered, which a `then` step cannot check
    │ 
    │ Help: move it to a `given` step before the request that makes the call
────╯
